+## Confining the files an agent reaches
+
+```sh
+gridcraft-cli mcp --automation-read-root ~/agent/in --automation-write-root ~/agent/out
+```
+
+The headless server's commands then open and load files (workbooks, CSV and JSON data, pictures)
+only from inside the read root, and save and export them only inside the write root. Each flag is
+`--flag DIR` or `--flag=DIR`, given once; the folder must exist. A root left out grants no access
+of its kind (with only a read root, nothing can be saved to a file). Paths are made absolute and
+their links followed before they are compared by whole folder names (without regard to case on
+Windows), so `..`, a sibling with the same prefix or a link out of the root is refused, with an
+`automation path rejected: …` or `automation filesystem access is not granted: …` error, and
+nothing is written outside. `--in FILE` is opened before the roots apply. The roots don't confine
+a running app: with `--connect` they are refused. A program that can change the folders while a
+command runs can still race the check; the roots keep an agent to the files it was given.
+
